{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Engine comparison RE-RUN (antifungal-amenable-mite), recorded 2026-11-12 02:27 PST. It supersedes the 00:05 PST run in my previous comment.\n\nWhy the re-run: LLM-Review on Gerrit 3366 caught that the first run titled every disposable ticket \"engine comparison <id>\". That title disagreed with each plan, and both engines flagged the mismatch. The harness now uses each ticket's real title from the tracker. Same corpus (digest c386161d43b1…), same 11 rows, AWS_PROFILE=frontier-bedrock.\n\nResults (src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/engine_comparison_results.json, valid=true, no errors, floor blocks or INDETERMINATEs):\n- Verdict agreement: 10/11 (0.91). Confusion matrix (pipeline rows × agentic columns): PASS→PASS 9, PASS→BLOCK 1, BLOCK→BLOCK 1, BLOCK→PASS 0.\n- Blocking flips: 1. The agentic engine blocked one plan the pipeline passed.\n- Finding overlap (token-set Jaccard ≥ 0.5, DET excluded): 1 matched, 102 pipeline-only, 58 agentic-only. This is a lexical lower bound: the engines word findings very differently.\n- Agreement with the historical pipeline verdict (10 decided rows): pipeline 6/10, agentic 5/10.\n\nThe title artifact had inflated disagreement: the 00:05 run showed 8/11 and 3 flips."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794479565481751450,"uuid":"94aafd14-1416-4e2b-881d-709d8a062cb7"}